uta-mechanistic-calibration

Third-party component
---------------------
external/network-wave-transmission-master/ contains the uterine-artery wave
transmission solver of Clark and colleagues, retained unmodified as downloaded
and distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see the LICENSE file in
that folder).

Source: https://github.com/VirtualPregnancy/network-wave-transmission (Apache License 2.0), commit 3d93afea5edc4f408240f11062a83a8c2d3f678d
(9 September 2020). The five files copied here (FunctionDefinitions.py, VesselDefinition.py, RUNME.py, LICENSE, README.md) are
byte-identical to that commit.

Reference: Clark AR, James JL, Stevenson GN, Collins SL. Understanding abnormal
uterine artery Doppler waveforms: a novel computational model to explore
potential causes within the utero-placental vasculature. Placenta.
2018;66:74-81. doi:10.1016/j.placenta.2018.05.001

All changes needed to run the solver with modern Python and to extract
waveform metrics are made in a separate adapter (code/solver_adapter.py); the
solver source itself has not been changed.
